# Copy to apps/mobile/.env. Expo reads the .env beside the app it is building,
# not the one at the repository root - the root file is the two backend
# services' and the web builds'.
#
# Only EXPO_PUBLIC_ variables reach the bundle; anything else here stays on the
# machine that ran the build.

# Where the accounts API is, as seen FROM THE DEVICE - which is the whole reason
# this variable exists and the web has no twin for it. A browser shares an
# origin with the API (apps/shell/vite.config.ts proxies /api to 3001), and a
# phone shares nothing.
#
#   iOS simulator      http://localhost:3001      - it shares the Mac's loopback
#   Android emulator   http://10.0.2.2:3001       - 10.0.2.2 IS the host machine
#   real device        http://<your-lan-ip>:3001  - and the API has to listen on
#                                                   0.0.0.0, not localhost
#
# `yarn start` is what puts that API on 3001.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3001

# Where the app reports errors and traces. Unset means Sentry stays off (see
# src/sentry.ts), which is what the tests and a plain `yarn mobile:start` want.
# A project of its own, the way each web build has one: a native stack trace is
# symbolicated from dSYMs and ProGuard maps that only this app produces.
# Project: alexisregnaud/demo-mobile-frontend
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=
